---
import GuideLayout from '../../layouts/GuideLayout.astro';
---

<GuideLayout slug="block-youtube-ads-free">
  <div class="gx-guide">
    <div class="gx-hero">
      <p class="gx-hero__kicker">Still free in 2026</p>
      <p class="gx-hero__line">
        The practical desktop route is <strong>AdBlock-Maxxer</strong>: download it, load the extracted
        folder into your browser's extensions page, turn it on, and refresh YouTube. Easiest alternative:
        a blocking browser like <strong>Brave</strong>.
      </p>
      <div class="gx-glance">
        <span class="gx-chip"><span class="gx-chip__i">🆓</span> $0</span>
        <span class="gx-chip"><span class="gx-chip__i">🖥</span> Desktop = best</span>
        <span class="gx-chip"><span class="gx-chip__i">📱</span> Mobile asterisk</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p class="gx-intro">
      AdBlock-Maxxer is a free, unpacked extension for Chrome, Brave, and Edge. It uses maintained filter
      lists for normal ad blocking. The optional <strong>YouTube Reclaim</strong>
      companion is only for accounts that hit server-side ad walls. Here is the actual setup, plus the honest
      limits on phones.
    </p>

    <h2>🥇 The two free routes that work</h2>
    <div class="gx-steps">
      <div class="gx-step">
        <div class="gx-step__num">1</div>
        <div class="gx-step__body">
          <h3>A blocking browser (easiest)</h3>
          <p>The lowest-effort route is a browser that blocks ads on its own — <strong>Brave</strong> being
            the obvious pick. Nothing to install, ads gone out of the box, works on phones too.</p>
          <p class="gx-note">⚠️ Trade-off: you're switching browsers, and built-in blockers sometimes lag a day or two behind YouTube's changes.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="gx-step">
        <div class="gx-step__num">2</div>
        <div class="gx-step__body">
          <h3>Install AdBlock-Maxxer (most control)</h3>
          <p>Open the <a href="/adblockmaxxer/">AdBlock-Maxxer page</a>, download the current browser ZIP,
            and <strong>unzip it somewhere permanent</strong>. Do not delete or move that folder after you
            install it — the browser loads the extension from there.</p>
          <p>Open <code>chrome://extensions</code>, <code>brave://extensions</code>, or
            <code>edge://extensions</code>. Turn on <strong>Developer mode</strong>, click
            <strong>Load unpacked</strong>, and choose the extracted folder that contains <code>manifest.json</code>.</p>
          <p>Click the puzzle-piece menu and pin the AdBlock-Maxxer shield. Click the shield, make sure the
            YouTube blocking toggle is on, then <strong>refresh any YouTube tab that was already open</strong>.
            Normal YouTube, Spotify, Twitch, and wider-web blocking now work without the companion.</p>
          <p class="gx-note">🔄 Updating: replace the extracted files with the newest ZIP, then click the browser's refresh icon on the extension card.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="gx-callout">
      <p class="gx-callout__tag">🎯 Check the install before judging it</p>
      <ul class="gx-mini">
        <li><strong>It should be enabled for the current site</strong> — click the shield and confirm YouTube blocking is on.</li>
        <li><strong>Refresh after installing or updating</strong> — a tab that was open before the extension loaded will not be retroactively changed.</li>
        <li><strong>Keep the folder intact</strong> — this is an unpacked install, so deleting or moving it disables the extension.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="gx-callout gx-callout--cyan">
      <p class="gx-callout__tag">📱 The mobile asterisk</p>
      <p>
        Desktop extensions don't run on iPhone Safari or inside the YouTube app. On your phone, the free
        options are a blocking browser (Brave) or, on iPhone, a browser like Orion that supports extensions.
        The YouTube app itself can't be extended — there's no free, no-jailbreak way to kill in-app ads that
        lasts. Watch in a browser instead.
      </p>
    </div>

    <h2>🛡 What about "anti-adblock" warnings?</h2>
    <p>
      When YouTube flashes "ad blockers aren't allowed," it's <em>detecting</em> your blocker — not beating
      it. First refresh the page and make sure the extension is enabled. If the video still black-screens or
      shows an <strong>"allow ads" wall</strong> on your account, that is server-side enforcement and a normal
      extension cannot remove it by itself.
    </p>

    <div class="gx-callout gx-callout--cyan">
      <p class="gx-callout__tag">🛠 Server-side ad wall? Add YouTube Reclaim</p>
      <p>
        Download the optional companion from the <a href="/adblockmaxxer/">AdBlock-Maxxer page</a>,
        unzip it, and double-click <code>abm-companion.exe</code> once. Keep its folder together, leave the
        extension's <strong>YouTube Reclaim</strong> toggle on, and retry the video. The companion runs locally;
        you do not need Python, and you do not need it for normal YouTube, Twitch, or Spotify blocking.
      </p>
    </div>

    <p class="gx-outro">
      <strong>Rule of thumb:</strong> start with the extension, turn it on, and refresh the page. Add the
      companion only for a server-side ad wall, and only download it from the official Maxxtopia page. That
      keeps the setup free, understandable, and reversible.
    </p>
  </div>
</GuideLayout>
